{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer","id":1482205,"title":"Scion: Sorcerer?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-28T17:20:53-07:00","id":1482205,"title":"Scion: Sorcerer?","content":"So, if Dragon is successful, and it looks like it will be, what does that mean for potential other scion spinoffs focusing on different supernatural critters in The World? Personally I wouldn't be surprised if they made a book about magic users, probably called Sorcerer to differentiate it from the WoD's Mage. What do folks around here think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T17:22:58-07:00","id":1482206,"title":"","content":"There's a book coming called Saint and Monsters,it will have a lot on sorcerers too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T17:25:00-07:00","id":1482207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482206#post1482206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a book coming called Saint and Monsters,it will have a lot on sorcerers too</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but with the raw magical potential inherent to the idea of wizards living in god-world, I wouldn't be surprised to see them doing a WoD style &quot;Well there's magic, and then there's <i>Magic</i>&quot; sort of setup. Feels like a waste of potential to make them just a denizen path ya know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T18:46:36-07:00","id":1482212,"title":"","content":"Several traditions have interesting twists on Sorcerers. Neoplatonic theurgists held that every human held a spark of divinity and thus humans could become gods through Theurgic Sorcery. Several Hindu myths have people and others gaining godlike power through profound austerities. One Egyptian myth says that Isis was a mortal woman who tricked Ra into telling her his most secret name. And by the power of that name she achieved godhood through sorcery. Humans becoming gods through sorcery isn't a universal trope, but it is widespread. A Scion: Sorcerer sounds like a great idea to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T19:11:53-07:00","id":1482214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482212#post1482212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several traditions have interesting twists on Sorcerers. Neoplatonic theurgists held that every human held a spark of divinity and thus humans could become gods through Theurgic Sorcery. Several Hindu myths have people and others gaining godlike power through profound austerities. One Egyptian myth says that Isis was a mortal woman who tricked Ra into telling her his most secret name. And by the power of that name she achieved godhood through sorcery. Humans becoming gods through sorcery isn't a universal trope, but it is widespread. A Scion: Sorcerer sounds like a great idea to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If nothing else it would be interesting to see how the magic system would work in a way that would differentiate it from Scions and Dragons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T23:38:50-07:00","id":1482221,"title":"","content":"With<b> Saints and Monsters</b> on the way, I predict that we will not see Sorcerers book in long time, if any. It's because <b>S&amp;M </b><i>already</i> has one full chapter on Sorcerers and their traditions. Here are previews we have to this date on subject:<br /> <br /> Sorcerers preview - <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/scion-saints-monsters-preview-4/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/scion-saints-monsters-preview-4/</a><br /> <br /> I will probably add Sorcerers to Scion World as larger players in way of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> multicultural Orders. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/scion-saints-monsters-preview-4/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1452937-cod-monsters-in-scion?p=1452956#post1452956\"><b>Datawaver</b> made great sum-up post how to make this</a> - later on we talk more more about this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-29-2022, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T05:16:44-07:00","id":1482242,"title":"","content":"That sum-up post was specifically about how to port <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> into <b>Scion</b>. That is <i>not</i> what I'd want to see from a <b>Dragon</b>-like <b>Scion: Mage</b> book. <br /> <br /> For <i>that</i>, I'd want something that focuses on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1424455-esotericism-in-scion?p=1425136#post1425136\">magic in the context of <b>Scion</b></a>. <br /> <br /> I'm very much looking forward to the <b>Saints and Monsters</b> book, in no small part because of the Sorcerers chapter. I don't think that we <i>need</i> a separate magic system for the World; the Purviews of the Gods work quite well for Sorcery, which in <b>Scion</b> is defined as \u201cborrowing\u201d the power of the gods. So no need for anything like \u201cDragon Magic\u201d \u2014 though since we <i>have</i> it, I wouldn't be against sorcerers who \u201csteal\u201d Inheritance to wield Dragon Magic instead of \u201cstealing\u201d Legend to wield Purviews. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> That said: if I were to do mages in <b>Scion</b>, as opposed to the power-thieving sorcerers in <b>Saints and Monsters</b>, I'd use <b>Masks of the Mythos</b> as my basis, at least in terms of game systems. Conceptually, Awareness isn't all that different from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Gnosis, once you scrape off the Cosmic Horror elements that the Mythos brings with it:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Awareness represents the opening of the mind and body to hidden realities that lurk just beyond human and non-<s>Mythos</s><span style=\"color:blue\">Supernal</span> Scions' senses. Contact with the <s>Mythos</s><span style=\"color:blue\">Supernal</span> changes people. It opens doors. It shifts one's point of view. It disrupts one's core understanding of how the universe works, and humanity's place in that <s>miasma</s><span style=\"color:blue\">Lie</span>. The disruption if the <s>Mythos</s><span style=\"color:blue\">Supernal</span> is beyond labels of good or bad, of evil or righteousness. The effect is expansive. The mind can adapt to these new understandings in a range of ways, but the resulting transformation can rarely be reversed.</div>The above quote is from <b>Masks of the Mythos</b>; but I've crossed out \u201cMythos\u201d and replaced it with \u201cSupernal\u201d (from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>) to make my point.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A character's Awareness rating generates a pool of Awareness points equal to the character's Awareness dots. Just like Legend, these points may be imbued or spent. Awareness is rated 1 to 10, and a Scion's Awareness rating does not change her divine quality. For example, a Scion with Legend 3 is still a Hero, even if her Awareness is 5.</div>In the context of mages, that would mean that it's possible to have significant Awareness and <i>no</i> Legend; though you'd miss out on Feats of Scale (since the bonus for Feats of Scale explicitly comes from Legend, even when Awareness is involved), and you'd <i>have to</i> take the Awareness Innate Powers for your Purviews, as you wouldn't have any Legend to give you access to the usual Innate Powers. <br /> <br /> The single biggest change I'd make here would be that a mage isn't beholden to the Mythos Pantheon. You'd likely have to invent one or more \u201cPantheons\u201d to empower mages through Awareness of their mysteries; I could, for example, see repurposing <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/342090\" target=\"_blank\">the Spiritual Hierarchy of the Ascended Masters</a> to work off of Awareness instead of Legend. Or perhaps the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/321122\" target=\"_blank\">New Gods</a>, if you want to allow for something like <b>Ascension</b>'s Technomancers. <br /> <br /> And the \u201cPantheon\u201d needn't involve personalities; all that's really needed is an organizing principle around which sets of Callings and Purviews can be arranged. For instance, the New Gods are kind of like this. And if you were to try to implement Kaballah in this manner, you might want to use the Sephirah in place of the Divine Patrons, assigning three Callings and a set of Purviews to each Sephiroth (though if I recall correctly, Kaballah has an Archangel watching over each Sephiroth; so you might as well just use those). And, of course, there would be the Signature Purview: Arcane Calculus for the Mythos; Psionics for the Ascended Masters; Materialism for the New Gods; and so on. In effect, your choice of Pantheon is your chosen style of magic. <br /> <br /> And you don't <i>necessarily</i> have to invent new Pantheons; I could see, for instance, tapping into Norse-style magic without becoming a Scion of the Aesir by developing Awareness of the Aesir, treating the Pantheon as a sort of mysticism and its gods as esoteric symbols rather than real people. It's not something that said gods would <i>appreciate</i>, mind you; and you'd probably be lumped in with the sorcerers as far as the gods view you. But you technically wouldn't be a sorcerer. In fact, you could probably combine the two, using Awareness as your mainstay and supplementing it with Sorcery-style Legend for the likes of Feats of Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-29-2022, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T07:01:44-07:00","id":1482248,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that the Neoplatonic Theurgists, who inspired &quot;Ars Magical&quot; and thus the WoD are your best bet. After all that paradigm implies divinity in all mortals and gaining godlike powers from your own inherent divinity. It's the clear link between Mage:tA and Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T07:47:05-07:00","id":1482250,"title":"","content":"While I wouldn't mind a \u201cPantheon\u201d (note the quotes) to facilitate Neoplatonic Theurgists, my point is that we can do much of the \u201cmage\u201d stuff with the tools that we already have on hand. Just using the existing Pantheons, their Motifs, and their Signature Purviews covers a lot of ground. The Netjer give us Egyptian magicians wielding Heku by speaking the sacred ritual words to release Sekhem, lending power to the soul; the Aesir give us Nordic magicians wielding the Wyrd by drawing runes or weaving threads; the Deva give us Indian mystics who chant spells and undergo austerities to wield the power of Yoga; the Tuatha use verse and satire to lay Geasa; and so on. We <i>already</i> have a diversity of options; and saying that we need to go with just one to represent mages just feels wrong. What a <b>Scion: Mage</b> ought to do, in my opinion, would be to present \u201cPantheons\u201d for those magical traditions that <i>don't</i> neatly align with existing Pantheons. Neoplatonic Theurgy would be one such example; Kaballah would be another; Theosophy too. Even Wicca might apply; I don't think there's a single Pantheon that can lay claim to it. <br /> <br /> More generally, I'm <i>not</i> thinking in terms of porting MtA into <b>Scion</b>; I'm thinking in terms of expanding <b>Scion</b> to also handle magical traditions that aren't aligned with individual Pantheons. If that lets you cover the same sort of ground that MtA covers, so much the better; but I see that as a fringe benefit, not a central goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-15-2022, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T09:34:40-07:00","id":1482258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482250#post1482250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More generally, I'm <i>not</i> thinking in terms of porting MtA into <b>Scion</b>; I'm thinking in terms of expanding <b>Scion</b> to also handle magical traditions that aren't aligned with individual Pantheons. If that lets you cover the same sort of ground that MtA covers, so much the better; but I see that as a fringe benefit, not a central goal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I feel that this is taking the wrong approach. The idea would be to use mortal magic users as a scion <i>spinoff</i>, a seperate kind of heroic being taking place in the same universe. If dragons are not just a reskinned pantheon, why should wizards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:19:16-07:00","id":1482262,"title":"","content":"You're missing my point. I'm not suggesting that Wizards* should be a reskinned Pantheon. But you don't need to reinvent the wheel, either. <br /> <br /> Dragons are as different from the gods as they are because part of the premise of <b>Scion: Dragon</b> is that they <i>predate</i> the gods, by hundreds of thousands of years. And they're not just outside of the order that the gods established; they're directly <i>opposed</i> to it. Thus, the Flights and the Dragon Magic instead of the Pantheons and the Purviews. <br /> <br /> Now, I'm not opposed to Wizards being organized in a manner that doesn't always align with the Pantheons; I could see Wizards being grouped into Practices (like High Ritual Magic, Witchcraft, Shamanism, etc.) as an alternative to Pantheons. But the existing Motifs and Signature Purviews of the Pantheons <i>also</i> lend themselves quite nicely to defining Practices, and I see no reason to get rid of them just for the sake of making Wizards different. <br /> <br /> And the Purviews are something else that I see no point in getting rid of just for the sake of being different. <br /> <br /> Finally, switching Legend out for Awareness is a pretty big change, conceptually. In some ways, it's an even bigger change than <b>Dragon</b>'s substitution of Inheritance for Legend. Frankly, I really don't see how one can reasonably characterize what I've described as \u201creskinning a Pantheon\u201d. <br /> <br /> * I really like \u201cWizard\u201d for this concept, BTW. Nicely keeps it distinct from both Mage and Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:34:10-07:00","id":1482266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482262#post1482262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing my point. I'm not suggesting that Wizards* should be a reskinned Pantheon. But you don't need to reinvent the wheel, either.<br /> <br /> Dragons are as different from the gods as they are because part of the premise of <b>Scion: Dragon</b> is that they <i>predate</i> the gods, by hundreds of thousands of years. And they're not just outside of the order that the gods established; they're directly <i>opposed</i> to it. Thus, the Flights and the Dragon Magic instead of the Pantheons and the Purviews.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not opposed to Wizards being organized in a manner that doesn't always align with the Pantheons; I could see Wizards being grouped into Practices (like High Ritual Magic, Witchcraft, Shamanism, etc.) as an alternative to Pantheons. But the existing Motifs and Signature Purviews of the Pantheons <i>also</i> lend themselves quite nicely to defining Practices, and I see no reason to get rid of them just for the sake of making Wizards different.<br /> <br /> And the Purviews are something else that I see no point in getting rid of just for the sake of being different.<br /> <br /> Finally, switching Legend out for Awareness is a pretty big change, conceptually. In some ways, it's an even bigger change than <b>Dragon</b>'s substitution of Inheritance for Legend. Frankly, I really don't see how one can reasonably characterize what I've described as \u201creskinning a Pantheon\u201d.<br /> <br /> * I really like \u201cWizard\u201d for this concept, BTW. Nicely keeps it distinct from both Mage and Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally believe that maybe a sort of semi-freeform system would work best. Something between purviews and arcanum. But the different traditions thing is not a bad idea. Hell most Onyx Path games with the storypath system use that, even They Came From has the archetypes and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:48:30-07:00","id":1482270,"title":"","content":"The Purviews are plenty freeform; that's what Marvels are all about. It's just that Heroes aren't the best at making use of Marvels. Demigods are considerably better at it, and I suspect that Gods will take it up another notch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T10:53:21-07:00","id":1482272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482270#post1482270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Purviews are plenty freeform; that's what Marvels are all about. It's just that Heroes aren't the best at making use of Marvels. Demigods are considerably better at it, and I suspect that Gods will take it up another notch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One could probably make it where that's the whole thing wizards do, marvels, just not as powerful. Like they're better at it to start than Heroes but don't have boons or other superpowers. What can I say I'm a sucker for spellcrafting mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T11:01:19-07:00","id":1482273,"title":"","content":"To put how I would explain the tone: If Mage The Awakening in the CofD is Dresden Files or a supernaturally-powered Matrix, then Scion: Wizard would be Dr. Strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","user":"Storyteller323","date":". 05-29-2022, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T15:00:17-07:00","id":1482290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482273#post1482273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put how I would explain the tone: If Mage The Awakening in the CofD is Dresden Files or a supernaturally-powered Matrix, then Scion: Wizard would be Dr. Strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of culturally distinctive sorcerers. I simply pointed out the pre existing link between Mage: the Ascension and Scion. I'd prefer playing a mage like Thessaly in Sandman. Someone who could connect to many different cultures or paradigms as they choose. Remember Thessaly delt with the Gods on a far stronger footing than most mortals, and some deities she knew she could boss around. <br /> <br /> I see two basic categories, shamans who bargain with the deities of their culture, and Thaumaturgists who are independent of individual pantheons. Even in North America Joseph Campbell reported a wide variety of attitudes toward shamans. Some cultures revered them, others considered them diabolical, still others thought their powers real but basically a joke. Some pantheons will gladly work with Sorcerers, others dispise them, and there would be a wide range of attitudes between. Thaumaturgists, as independent powers would also get a wide range of reactions too. Probably more cautious ones.<br /> <br /> Within each category their would be multiple subcategories. Bards, Druids, Faery Doctors, were all Celtic, all fit my particular take on Shaman, but they're profoundly different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-29-2022, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T16:53:06-07:00","id":1482307,"title":"","content":"One of the things that <b>Scion</b> is known for is its culturally accurate and culturally specific Pantheons. Especially in 2e, efforts have been made to \u201cget it right, or not at all\u201d. I would expect something similar for this hypothetical <b>Scion: Wizard</b> book: rather than going with broad, generic categories like \u201canimists and thaumaturges\u201d, I'd expect a series of culturally specific magical Practices, some of which align with Pantheons and others that don't. <br /> <br /> In the former case, I could see using this to provide some clarity and/or corrections to the way the existing Pantheon Motifs and Signature Purviews work. For instance, I could see providing <i>two</i> Shen-related Practices: one that features the Shen Motif but features its own Signature Purview (or no Signature Purview at all), and another that features the Shen Signature Purview but works through a different Motif. <br /> <br /> And speaking of Motifs, I'd like to see each of the Motifs expanded from a single sentence to a paragraph or two \u2014 something comparable to the Practice write-ups found in M20: start with the Motif's defining sentence, then follow that up with practical advice of what that looks like in play, and maybe a address a few of the finer points of the theory behind the Motif. <br /> <br /> And just like <b>Scion</b> resists the urge to, say, lump everyone in North America into a single hybridized \u201cNative American Pantheon\u201d, I'd want even the Practices that <i>don't</i> align with Pantheons to be culturally specific, accurate, and respectful: we've come a long way from the early 90s, when <b>Ascension</b> presented us with nine Traditions that were based on broad stereotypes of different kinds of magic users; and while <b>Ascension</b> has subsequently shown itself to be very adept at making lemonade out of the lemons it started out with, <b>Scion</b> (2e in particular) has the potential to get it right from the start.<br /> <br /> In particular, there's no need to try to come up with counterparts to <b>Ascension</b>'s Dreamspeakers and Verbena: the Practices that closely align with Pantheons take care of most of that business. More generally, I don't think that <i>any</i> of the hypothetical <b>Scion: Wizard</b>'s Practices should be anywhere near as broad as <b>Ascension</b>'s Traditions. If broad categories exist at all, they should be presented in a \u201cbottom up\u201d approach, starting with culturally specific Practices and then mentioning some commonalities between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T19:47:20-07:00","id":1482321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482262#post1482262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not opposed to Wizards being organized in a manner that doesn't always align with the Pantheons; I could see Wizards being grouped into Practices (like High Ritual Magic, Witchcraft, Shamanism, etc.) as an alternative to Pantheons. But the existing Motifs and Signature Purviews of the Pantheons <i>also</i> lend themselves quite nicely to defining Practices, and I see no reason to get rid of them just for the sake of making Wizards different.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you are literally now reinventing Paths from <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> With Magic based on Purviews, not simpler Arcana, you basiclly have most of Paths ideal as 'magical general practice' and 'Awakening Supernal story' ( strife for Mastigos, breaking paterns for Acanthus, etc ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only let character to have more than one Signature Purvies of Pantheons - and you are set for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482262#post1482262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Purviews are something else that I see no point in getting rid of just for the sake of being different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree - I run <b>Scion: Hero</b> game about year now - and I can say that Purviews in day-to-day use works more or less like Arcana in Creative Thaumaturgy aspects ( with Marvels and Relics ), but are also much more 'style/practice bounded' than Arcana, for example. My <b>Scion</b> players are making <b>M:tAw</b>-like rituals on left and right if they need Marvel in story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482262#post1482262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, switching Legend out for Awareness is a pretty big change, conceptually. In some ways, it's an even bigger change than <b>Dragon</b>'s substitution of Inheritance for Legend. Frankly, I really don't see how one can reasonably characterize what I've described as \u201creskinning a Pantheon\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still would use Gnosis as term, instead of Awerness - it's shorter, more ear-catchy - and means almost the same. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482262#post1482262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I really like \u201cWizard\u201d for this concept, BTW. Nicely keeps it distinct from both Mage and Sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wizard would be Harry Dresden, really. Sorcerer is, by dictionary definition, someone who bargins with gods for powers - literally. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T19:50:29-07:00","id":1482322,"title":"","content":"As the person who wrote most of the Sorcerer section of Saints &amp; Monsters, I will only suggest remembering Scion focuses on myth and folklore rather than philosophy.<br /> <br /> But these are interesting ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T19:53:01-07:00","id":1482324,"title":"","content":"I still would point out that if you let character use multiple Signature Purviews of Pantheons - and I think you should, to make them more distinct from normal Scions - you are literally make characters that dwells into 'secrets of the World', by wraping with few distinctive Truths ( i.e. Cosmologies ) that each Pantheon represents. You basically make <b>M:tAw</b> characters <i>without</i> idea of Supernal ( or maybe background of it ), as characters are then comb through the various - seemingly CONFLICTING - Truths and use them as they please. \ud83d\ude2e<br /> <br /> <b>MtAw</b>-like characters, here you go! \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-29-2022, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:16:35-07:00","id":1482327,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rather stick to a maximum of one Signature Purview per Wizard; but you do you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:18:36-07:00","id":1482328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482322#post1482322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the person who wrote most of the Sorcerer section of Saints &amp; Monsters, I will only suggest remembering Scion focuses on myth and folklore rather than philosophy.<br /> <br /> But these are interesting ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I think it might work better as a Nexus product than as an official product. And if I had the time and skills to write it myself, I would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:29:37-07:00","id":1482332,"title":"","content":"Mechanically - Limit their use of Knacks only ever to Origin level and no inner Feat of Scale - but give them possibility to use Legend/Awerness/Gnosis times Marvels per scene.<br /> <br /> And voila - MtAw Sorcerers like you see. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T20:51:50-07:00","id":1482334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482321#post1482321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know you are literally now reinventing Paths from <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> With Magic based on Purviews, not simpler Arcana, you basiclly have most of Paths ideal as 'magical general practice' and 'Awakening Supernal story' ( strife for Mastigos, breaking paterns for Acanthus, etc ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only let character to have more than one Signature Purvies of Pantheons - and you are set for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I took the \u201cHigh Ritual/Witchcraft/Shamanism\u201d examples from <b>Ascension</b>, not <b>Awakening</b>. If I were inclined to use this to model <b>Awakening</b>, I'd do so entirely within the context of a single \u201cHigh Ritual\u201d or \u201cNeoplatonic Theurgy\u201d Practice, with the Oracles as the \u201cGods\u201d of that Practice. <br /> <br /> But that strikes me as not \u201cMythology and Folklore\u201d enough for my liking, and <i>way</i> too derivative of <b>Awakening</b>: like I said earlier, I'm not interested in porting <b>Awakening</b> into <b>Scion</b>. I'd rather research \u201cNeoplatonic Theurgy\u201d, figure out what if anything that Practice views as its \u201cgods\u201d, and use <i>them</i>. A lot more authentic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T02:52:32-07:00","id":1482356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482334#post1482334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I took the \u201cHigh Ritual/Witchcraft/Shamanism\u201d examples from <b>Ascension</b>, not <b>Awakening</b>. If I were inclined to use this to model <b>Awakening</b>, I'd do so entirely within the context of a single \u201cHigh Ritual\u201d or \u201cNeoplatonic Theurgy\u201d Practice, with the Oracles as the \u201cGods\u201d of that Practice. <br /> <br /> But that strikes me as not \u201cMythology and Folklore\u201d enough for my liking, and <i>way</i> too derivative of <b>Awakening</b>: like I said earlier, I'm not interested in porting <b>Awakening</b> into <b>Scion</b>. I'd rather research \u201cNeoplatonic Theurgy\u201d, figure out what if anything that Practice views as its \u201cgods\u201d, and use <i>them</i>. A lot more authentic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neoplatonic Theurgists used any and all gods known to the late classical world. Neoplatonism viewed all the gods as aspects of God. It was both pantheistic and monotheistic at the same time. I brought them up as they were A) the inspiration for most Western ideas of Wizards and Magicians, and B) their beliefs click fairly well with Scion as they are magicians focused on divinity. They believed all humans have an internal spark of divinity and can ascend to godhood. Since Scions literally ascend to godhood it seemed like a close fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T18:49:30-07:00","id":1482434,"title":"","content":"Honestly at this point rather than giving mechanic ideas it's just fun to watch yall debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:31:24-07:00","id":1482562,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver look up Hermes Trimagistos ( I probably misspelled that). He's a syncretic deity Greece/Egypt. A combination of Hermes and Thoth. Also look up the Corpus Hermeticam and the Emerald Tablet of Hermes Trimagistos. There's a book Egyptian Hermes that should give you a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:34:09-07:00","id":1482603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1482205-scion-sorcerer?p=1482334#post1482334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that strikes me as not \u201cMythology and Folklore\u201d enough for my liking, and <i>way</i> too derivative of <b>Awakening</b>: like I said earlier, I'm not interested in porting <b>Awakening</b> into <b>Scion</b>. I'd rather research \u201cNeoplatonic Theurgy\u201d, figure out what if anything that Practice views as its \u201cgods\u201d, and use <i>them</i>. A lot more authentic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iamblichus' account of Neoplatonic theurgy is the standard. You can read it here: <a href=\"http://www.esotericarchives.com/oracle/iambl_th.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.esotericarchives.com/oracle/iambl_th.htm</a><br /> <br /> For Hermetism (i.e., the Graeco-Egyptian teachings, as distinct from later Hermeticism), you can find the Corpus Hermeticum online fairly easily. I'll second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>'s recommendation of Garth Fowden's <i>The Egyptian Hermes,</i> which provides some useful historical context for the philosophical Hermetica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}